==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
Possibly an ancient loan from {{proto|Indo-European|h₂awks-|lang=fi}}, with metathesis ''*kawsa-'' > {{proto|Finnic|kasva-|lang=fi}} (whence also eg. Estonian {{term|kasuda|lang=et}}, Livonian {{term|ka'zzõ|lang=liv}}, Votic {{term|kazvaa|lang=vot}}). The loan is shared with the Mordvinic languages (eg. Erzya {{term|касомс|tr=kasoms|lang=myv}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈkɑsvɑː(ʔ)/}}
* Rhymes: [[rasvaa]]
* {{hyphenation|kas|vaa}}

===Verb===
{{head|fi|verb}}
{{intransitive}} 

# To [[grow]].
# To [[increase]], [[increment]].
# To [[wax]] (of the Moon).

